{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00088",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 6.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Doctor, hello, I've got my papers here, where should I put them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.02,
      "end_seconds": 11.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "right on time sit, please how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.56,
      "end_seconds": 17.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "thank you for fitting us in, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.18,
      "end_seconds": 25.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.84,
      "end_seconds": 31.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Doctor, it's a very sore throat. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.32,
      "end_seconds": 35.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "How long are we talking about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.71,
      "end_seconds": 40.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "It's been ten days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.14,
      "end_seconds": 45.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "does anything bring it on or make it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.71,
      "end_seconds": 49.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I notice it more with swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.48,
      "end_seconds": 53.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "how much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.16,
      "end_seconds": 56.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.11,
      "end_seconds": 62.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 62.79,
      "end_seconds": 69.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.01,
      "end_seconds": 72.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "later, thanks. Please go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.23,
      "end_seconds": 78.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "I've, I've also had a fever, for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.03,
      "end_seconds": 91.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.08,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.93,
      "end_seconds": 97.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Severe, really. It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.53,
      "end_seconds": 105.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "have you had a very sore throat before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.11,
      "end_seconds": 112.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 113.96,
      "end_seconds": 116.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "mm, that's what happened, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.76,
      "end_seconds": 127.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "And what about cough, ear pain or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.94,
      "end_seconds": 140.9,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "so, no, no cough, no ear pain, no rash i did have swollen glands in the neck at one point, but that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.53,
      "end_seconds": 144.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Any runny nose or drooling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.37,
      "end_seconds": 149.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I haven't had runny nose or drooling, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.54,
      "end_seconds": 153.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "And difficulty breathing, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.45,
      "end_seconds": 156.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "no difficulty breathing, thankfully"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.74,
      "end_seconds": 160.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.52,
      "end_seconds": 163.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.74,
      "end_seconds": 167.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.64,
      "end_seconds": 171.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "no, that side's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.18,
      "end_seconds": 177.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Is there a family history of anything significant?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.25,
      "end_seconds": 181.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "My sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.08,
      "end_seconds": 188.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Are there any allergies on your record that I should check?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.93,
      "end_seconds": 199.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.84,
      "end_seconds": 202.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Do you work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.35,
      "end_seconds": 211.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "I run a small shop, so I'm on my feet a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.53,
      "end_seconds": 216.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "is anyone at home with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.27,
      "end_seconds": 220.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I share a flat with two friends"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.58,
      "end_seconds": 224.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "so, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.87,
      "end_seconds": 230.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "I had my tonsils out when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.1,
      "end_seconds": 234.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "what medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 235.91,
      "end_seconds": 243.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "She is on Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.27,
      "end_seconds": 247.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Okay, when did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 248.71,
      "end_seconds": 259.97,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "Nearly five years now. It's furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning for the fluid, doctor. She takes alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.72,
      "end_seconds": 264.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "When did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 266.11,
      "end_seconds": 268.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "About a month now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.84,
      "end_seconds": 280.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.17,
      "end_seconds": 289.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "I have asthma. I have heart failure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.2,
      "end_seconds": 291.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.5,
      "end_seconds": 296.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Thin bones, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 297.45,
      "end_seconds": 307.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pressure 118 over 71, SpO2 96 percent on room air, temperature 38.4, pulse 105."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.23,
      "end_seconds": 310.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.65,
      "end_seconds": 315.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "let's do the physical part now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.76,
      "end_seconds": 317.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "okay, ready"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.79,
      "end_seconds": 321.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "let me just check something"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.18,
      "end_seconds": 338.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "both tonsils are red and swollen, and there are white patches on the the left one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.89,
      "end_seconds": 340.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.47,
      "end_seconds": 344.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.4,
      "end_seconds": 357.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "The The glands under the jaw are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.42,
      "end_seconds": 381.31,
      "duration_seconds": 18.89,
      "text": "All done, you can get dressed. Okay, thinking it through, this is probably tonsillitis, probably bacterial. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out a viral throat infection yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.57,
      "end_seconds": 385.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.58,
      "end_seconds": 397.35,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with tonsillitis, probably bacterial do well once it's treated properly. Let's book a throat swab to look into sore throat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 398.32,
      "end_seconds": 403.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "We have a slot Monday at 11:30 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.45,
      "end_seconds": 406.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Monday, that works for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.7,
      "end_seconds": 435.61,
      "duration_seconds": 27.91,
      "text": "the treatment will be paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days that's for fever and body aches you'll be taking amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, for five days it's for throat infection finish the whole course of antibiotics even if you feel better after two days gargle with warm salt water a few times a day, it does soothe it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.45,
      "end_seconds": 446.52,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Book a review in a week. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.06,
      "end_seconds": 449.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, thanks."
    }
  ]
}